{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_014HciWXCub7Q1AicA3Wit85","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the workspace's `CLAUDE.md` and supporting docs, here's what this project **is**:\n\n- **It's John Liechty's \"Agentic Sandbox\"** (`C:\\dev\\Agentic-Home`) â€” a research workspace for building, training, and evaluating clusters of AI agents. It's explicitly a research project, not a production system; most of its ~80 root folders are design documents, with a smaller set of runnable code.\n\n- **The active shipped deliverable is the Ghost World Labs (GWL-M) master GUI** â€” a Next.js app (`sandbox-lab-gui/`) launched via `Launch-Ghost-World-Labs.bat`, which runs a custom Next.js + WebSocket server (`server.mjs`) and a dashboard that spawns/supervises agent terminals (Gemini CLI, Claude Code, and the Alpha agents).\n\n- **Agents run on the OpenClaw runtime** (MIT-licensed, global npm package). The GUI dispatches turns through `agent-chat.mjs` / `agent-chat-v0.mjs`, which read per-agent provider/model from the canonical `routing.json` and a skill bundle from a master skill repo (`skills-master/`).\n\n- **The headline architecture work is the \"t2r/t2rs\" brain + a brain-agnostic harness.** The harness (a clean ReAct loop with cost-aware tier routing, prompt caching, wallet caps, and verification gates) is being completed toward GA; three interchangeable \"brains\" plug into it â€” Opus-4.8 baseline, the efficient t2r brain, and a fully-local/sovereign ~7â€“8B OSS model on the RTX 4070.\n\n- **It ships a portable skill ecosystem** â€” reusable skills (expert-coder, research1/researchPrime, project-manager, deep-think, crucible, foreman, etc.) linked into Claude Code/Gemini via junctions and copied into OpenClaw, following a skillâ†’bundleâ†’specialistâ†’agent maturity ladder.\n\n- **The canonical home is the `gwl-server` box** (RTX 4070, 12 GB VRAM) â€” chosen specifically to unblock QLoRA fine-tuning of small local student models, distilling judgment from frontier models into sovereign local agents.\n\nOne caveat on grounding: these claims come from the `CLAUDE.md` orientation doc and memory index, not from independently reading the source tree. If you want, I can verify any specific claim (e.g., that the GUI server actually behaves as described) against the actual files."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7051,"cache_read_input_tokens":40827,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7051,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"21e6b796-8ba2-4de9-8f13-02b639a809c6","uuid":"129f94ca-3066-4fb8-b7c0-dbba9d8b6dde","request_id":"req_011Cc38oQ5PK7EArRVgAJ9UC"}
